{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Therefore</b> — לכן is from the root שכה, like it: \"הלא אתה שכת בעדו\"." "<b>In thorn-bushes</b> — בסירים, thorns, as in כי כקול הסירים and כי עד סירים סבוכים." "<b>Her paths</b> — נתיבותיה: the known places that have signs to recognize her." "<b>And I will wall up her wall</b> — וגדרתי את גדרה: that I will set a fence on her paths, like גדר דרכי בגזית."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The verse cited is Isaiah 42:22; Ibn Ezra argues לכן here derives from a root meaning 'to lie in wait,' not the usual 'therefore.'", 1 "Cited phrases are from Isaiah 9:17 (סירים = thorns) and Isaiah 34:13 respectively.", 2 "Rendered literally; Ibn Ezra explains the term as landmarks or path-markers for identification.", 3 "Cited phrase is from Lamentations 3:9."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:49:52.107055366Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}